    {
      "id": "s5nwezo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SUPREME COURT OF INDIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Supreme Court of India is the highest constitutional court and the ultimate apex judicial body in the country.",
        "Article 131 grants Original Jurisdiction to adjudicate disputes between the Centre and States or between different States.",
        "Article 32 confers Writ Jurisdiction directly upon the Supreme Court for the enforcement of Fundamental Rights.",
        "Article 143 gives Advisory Jurisdiction allowing the President of India to consult the court on legal and factual public questions.",
        "Article 142 equips the court with inherent powers to pass orders necessary for doing complete justice in any cause."
      ],
      "id": "y2snkro"
    },
