    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "High Court writ jurisdiction under Article 226 is broader than Supreme Court writ jurisdiction under Article 32, as High Courts can issue writs for legal rights beyond fundamental rights.",
        "Under Article 143, the opinion rendered by the Supreme Court in its advisory capacity is not binding on the President.",
        "Article 129 establishes the Supreme Court as a 'Court of Record', giving it the power to punish for contempt of itself."
      ],
      "id": "7x2ya6v"
